! Le Grand full theoretical eye, accommodated
! Generated by EveryEyeModel scripts/make_formats.py from data/; do not edit.
! Written by AI (Claude, by Anthropic) at Dan Gray's direction; values from the source below.
! Source: Y. Le Grand and S. G. El Hage, Physiological Optics (Springer, 1980); values as tabulated in J. Schwiegerling, 'Schematic Eyes and Ametropia', University of Arizona course notes. See models/le-grand-full-theoretical-eye.md.
! The source gives one set of indices and no wavelength; they are filed at 587.6 nm. The model has no dispersion: use one wavelength.
! The stop (iris) is placed at the lens front surface.
! The source gives no retina for the accommodated eye; the relaxed eye's retina (R = -13.4 mm) is used.
LEN NEW
TITLE 'Le Grand full theoretical eye, accommodated'
DIM M
EPD 4
WL 587.6
REF 1
XAN 0 0 0
YAN 0 10 20
PRV
PWL 587.6
'LGA_COR' 1.377100
'LGA_AQU' 1.337400
'LGA_LEN' 1.427000
'LGA_VIT' 1.336000
END
SO 0 1E+20
S 7.8 0.55 LGA_COR
S 6.5 2.65 LGA_AQU
S 6.0 4.5 LGA_LEN
  STO
S -5.5 16.497 LGA_VIT
SI -13.4 0
GO
